      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the woman in <Picture 1>. Her facial identity, facial structure, skin tone, hairstyle, age appearance, body type, and body proportions come exclusively from <Picture 1>. Her complete outfit, including its design, colors, materials, accessories, and footwear, comes exclusively from <Picture 2>. <Subject 1> is also the sole vocalist and speaker (S1).\n<Subject 2> is the background environment in <Picture 3>, including its architecture, spatial layout, decorative elements, lighting, color palette, and overall visual atmosphere.\n<Subject 3> is the confident rap performance executed by <Subject 1>, including precise Japanese lip synchronization, controlled head nods, expressive hand gestures, upper-body movement, and natural shifts in posture synchronized to the beat.\n<Picture 3> is the principal composition and environmental reference for the target video.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] Generate a 15-second music-video sequence featuring <Subject 1>, preserving the woman’s identity from <Picture 1> while transferring the complete outfit from <Picture 2> onto her. She performs a short Japanese rap in <Subject 2>, the background environment from <Picture 3>. Her mouth movements, expressions, gestures, and body rhythm remain precisely synchronized with the lyrics and a heavy hip-hop beat throughout the video.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears throughout the video): fully_preserved - the woman’s facial identity, facial structure, hairstyle, age appearance, body type, and body proportions from <Picture 1> remain consistent across every shot.\n<Subject 1> (outfit appearance): attribute_transfer - the complete clothing design, colors, materials, accessories, and footwear from <Picture 2> are transferred onto the woman without retaining clothing from <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 1> (Japanese rap vocal): fully_preserved - she performs only the specified Japanese lyrics in a confident female voice, with clear pronunciation and precise lip synchronization.\n<Subject 2> (appears throughout the video): fully_preserved - the background architecture, spatial arrangement, decorations, lighting, and color palette from <Picture 3> remain recognizable and visually consistent.\n<Subject 3> (rap performance): fully_preserved - confident expressions, rhythmic head nods, hand gestures, and body movement remain continuous and synchronized with the beat.\n<Picture 3> (environmental composition): partially_preserved - its background design and visual atmosphere are retained while the framing changes naturally between shots.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] Open with a stable medium frontal shot of <Subject 1> standing near the center of <Subject 2>. She has the exact facial identity, hairstyle, age appearance, body type, and proportions shown in <Picture 1>, while wearing the complete outfit from <Picture 2>. She looks directly into the camera and begins rapping with a focused, confident expression. Her mouth forms every Japanese syllable clearly and in precise synchronization with the beat. She performs controlled head nods and compact hand gestures while delivering the first line:\n<Subject 1> (S1): <d>[Japanese] 響く低音　街ごと揺らす</d>\nThe camera slowly pushes toward her while preserving the recognizable background, lighting, and color palette of <Picture 3>.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.500, cut to a low-angle three-quarter medium shot. The camera tracks laterally beside <Subject 1> as she continues without a pause. She maintains strong eye contact with the lens, marking the rhythm with sharper hand gestures and natural shoulder movement. She delivers the second line:\n<Subject 1> (S1): <d>[Japanese] 視線は前へ　迷いは捨てた</d>\nHer outfit remains identical to <Picture 2>, with realistic fabric and accessory movement. <Subject 2> stays spatially coherent behind her.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.000, cut to a close-up of <Subject 1> with subtle handheld camera movement and shallow depth of field. Her facial identity remains unmistakably consistent with <Picture 1>. Capture precise lip synchronization, small eyebrow movements, confident eye contact, and subtle facial tension as she delivers the third line:\n<Subject 1> (S1): <d>[Japanese] この声ひとつで　未来を照らす</d>\nThe lighting and colors from <Picture 3> remain visible as softly blurred environmental details behind her.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:10.500, cut to a wider three-quarter shot as the camera performs a smooth partial orbit around <Subject 1>. She increases the energy of her performance with broader but controlled arm gestures and a firm rhythmic stance. She turns back toward the lens and delivers the final line with her strongest expression:\n<Subject 1> (S1): <d>[Japanese] 今この瞬間　私が主役</d>\nThe orbit reveals more of <Subject 2> while maintaining its original architecture, decorations, illumination, and spatial arrangement. On the final word, she stops in a strong pose facing the camera as the last beat lands.\n\nThe four lyric lines must be delivered once, in the specified order, with no additional spoken words, improvised lyrics, repetition, or background vocals. Distribute the lyrics naturally across the full 15-second duration without rushing the pronunciation.\n\nAcross all shots, preserve single-subject continuity. <Subject 1> must remain the same woman from <Picture 1>, wearing only the outfit from <Picture 2>. Do not blend her facial or bodily characteristics with another person, do not revert to the clothing from <Picture 1>, and do not create duplicate performers. Maintain anatomically natural hands, facial features, clothing, and body movement.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nNatural environmental ambience appropriate to <Subject 2>, kept subtle beneath the vocal and music, with light spatial reflections and realistic movement sounds from clothing, accessories, and footsteps. The Japanese rap vocal remains clear, centered, and prominent in the mix.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA heavy, bass-driven hip-hop instrumental with deep sub-bass, hard punchy kick drums, crisp snare hits, sparse dark synth textures, and a steady confident groove. The rhythm supports the timing of the four Japanese lyric lines without overpowering the voice. Add a stronger final beat accent synchronized with <Subject 1>’s ending pose."
